---
/**
 * Book I, Ch. II, Prop. 2 — depth without non-linearity collapses. Left: two
 * linear maps composed, which is one line. Right: the same depth with a ReLU
 * between, which is a piecewise fold.
 */
---
<svg class="fig" viewBox="0 0 720 320" role="img" aria-labelledby="df-t df-d" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" style="--fig-min: 620px">
  <title id="df-t">Composition with and without a non-linearity</title>
  <desc id="df-d">
    On the left, two linear layers composed produce a single straight line: the
    stack collapses to one layer. On the right, the same two layers with a
    rectifier between them produce a piecewise-linear curve with three segments.
  </desc>

  <text x="0" y="22" class="t-lab">linear ∘ linear</text>
  <text x="392" y="22" class="t-lab">linear ∘ relu ∘ linear</text>

  <g>
    <line x1="30" y1="270" x2="330" y2="270" class="axis" />
    <line x1="30" y1="270" x2="30" y2="60" class="axis" />
    <line x1="42" y1="256" x2="318" y2="82" class="s1" stroke-width="1.6" />
    <text x="180" y="304" class="t-sm" text-anchor="middle">one line, whatever the depth</text>
  </g>

  <g>
    <line x1="392" y1="270" x2="692" y2="270" class="axis" />
    <line x1="392" y1="270" x2="392" y2="60" class="axis" />
    <polyline points="404,254 480,254 566,140 680,96" class="s2" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" />
    <circle cx="480" cy="254" r="3.4" class="a2" />
    <circle cx="566" cy="140" r="3.4" class="a2" />
    <line x1="480" y1="254" x2="480" y2="278" class="dash" />
    <line x1="566" y1="140" x2="566" y2="278" class="dash" />
    <text x="480" y="294" class="t-key" text-anchor="middle">kink</text>
    <text x="566" y="294" class="t-key" text-anchor="middle">kink</text>
    <text x="542" y="316" class="t-sm" text-anchor="middle">each unit contributes a fold</text>
  </g>
</svg>
